    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. Can you go into a bit more detail on the potential risks or \"hidden\" issues with horizontal scaling? Like, what usually goes wrong when you try to manage all those extra nodes at once?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The biggest hidden risks with horizontal scaling are system complexity and reliability; managing dozens or hundreds of individual nodes is much harder than tuning one machine. Common problems include lost state when distributing sessions across nodes or unexpected downtime if one \"truck\" in your convoy breaks without an immediate replacement. To mitigate this, you must invest in sophisticated monitoring and automation teams to ensure that software updates and failures are handled efficiently across the entire infrastructure.",
      "source": "target",
