    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Yeah, the complexity part is what I'm worried about. Sometimes things just seem to break for no reason, even when everything looks fine on the dashboard. Are there certain types of errors that are just harder to track down in a distributed system like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, distributed systems often suffer from subtle issues like \"Split Brains,\" where data appears inconsistent because different nodes hold slightly different versions of the same information. Tracking these errors is difficult because failures can happen randomly or silently, making it hard to pinpoint exactly what went wrong without detailed, automated instrumentation. To mitigate this, you should rely on dead-letter queues to catch failed tasks and ensure no data is lost or duplicated during load spikes.",
      "source": "target",
